: The Hindu --></div></div>",
    "content_text": "S\nickness never heralds its arrival, so buying medical insurance today ensures you are never caught off guard. Having been in the banking sector where medical expenses were cushioned to a certain extent, we retirees are now facing a financial crunch as we age.\nNothing is free today. Every year around the same time, retirees scramble to decide which insurance company has the most attractive offer. After the coronavirus visited the globe in a devastating manner in the year 2020, every hospitalisation has become a steep affair. Terms and conditions rolled out year-on-year for group insurance schemes vary. It fits well within the budget of some, while many have to prepare well in advance to pay off the stipulated amount.\nPublished\n- November 22, 2026 05:00 am IST\nCopy link\nEmail\nFacebook\nTwitter\nTelegram\nLinkedIn\nWhatsApp\nReddit\nREAD LATER\nSEE ALL\nRemove",
