    "title": "Curiosity versus cockiness",
    "subtitle": null,
    "author": "G.L.  Krishna",
    "published_at": null,
    "image_url": null,
    "image_caption": null,
    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71716914\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\"><p><span class=\"drop-caps\">C</span>uriosity is a genuinely good thing. When backed by sincerity and perseverance, it leads one towards the joy of understanding. At times, it leads even towards discovery and innovation. But when curiosity is backed by neither of these, it manifests as an attitude of questioning that is casual and leisurely at best, or cocky and disrespectful at worst.</p><p>Many a time, teenagers and young adults mistake cockiness for curious questioning. Given that achieving and asserting identity is a key task of adolescence, some amount of cockiness is perhaps natural for that age. Problems arise when it crosses a healthy threshold and begins to throttle a young person’s sincerity and perseverance. The questioning attitude should not morph into an attempt to do the precise opposite of what family and society think is proper and desirable. In other words, a healthy questioning attitude is not reactive; it is proactive born out of a sincere quest to learn and experience the joy of understanding.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- November 22, 2026 04:45 am IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71716914\" data-title=\"Curiosity versus cockiness\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/curiosity-versus-cockiness/article71716914.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-ab93aa43b91b447f1221532f-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/op