    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71716952\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\"><p><span class=\"drop-caps\">T</span>he weather was damp and cosy, which called for a hot cup of tea and some steaming savouries. We sat on our veranda, enjoying the downpour and relishing our snacks. While chit-chatting, we covered all the usual topics, including current affairs and trending gossip.</p><p>Suddenly, my mother noticed an unexpected visitor beside our chairs — a huge tortoise. It was hiding beneath its gigantic shell. Upon seeing us, the tortoise quickly retracted its neck into its shell, which was so beautifully patterned that it looked as if it had been customised by a designer. It remained hidden for some time; after observing that the surroundings were safe, it slowly extended its neck. It reminded me of those wise old tortoises in animated movies, the ones who always seem to have spectacles on their noses.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- November 22, 2026 04:30 am IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71716952\" data-title=\"The spectator from the past\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/the-spectator-from-the-past/article71716952.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-4c32c31ab3612c1ce55b7ed9-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/the-spectator-from-the-past/article71716952.ece');\">\n                Copy link  \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"email\"><a href=\"mailto:?subject=T