 End DFP : /22390678/TH_MWeb_AT_Middle05, publisher: The Hindu --></div></div>",
    "content_text": "D\nespite knowing full well that wars are notoriously internecine, there has been little or no let-up in global conflicts in recent years. From time to time, warring (and war-devastated) countries proclaim their readiness to bury the hatchet. However, few ever forget where it’s buried. And therein lies the crux of the matter.\nTo be meaningful, rapprochement should clearly spell out (and not merely imply) a genuine and sincere willingness to mutually forgive and resolutely breakaway from the barbaric practice of retribution or claiming an eye for an eye. True forgiveness is, in essence, a heart-soothing balm — in equal measure to both the survivor of a crime (or one affected by it) and the perpetrator.\nPublished\n- November 22, 2026 04:15 am IST\nCopy link\nEmail\nFacebook\nTwitter\nTelegram\nLinkedIn\nWhatsApp\nReddit\nREAD LATER\nSEE ALL\nRemove",
